{"tool_name":"flash","contents":["biocontainers","galaxy","bioschemas","debian","biotools","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"flash","identifiers":["biotools:flash","doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btr507"],"license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Merge mates from fragments that are shorter than twice the read length","home_url":"https://ccb.jhu.edu/software/FLASH/","keywords":["Chromosomes, Human, Pair 14","Genome","Genomics","Humans","Sequence Analysis, DNA","Staphylococcus aureus","Sequencing","Sequence assembly","RNA-Seq","Genetics","Transcriptome"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":3288},"biotools":{"id":"flash","home":"http://ccb.jhu.edu/software/FLASH/","summary":"Identifies paired-end reads which overlap in the middle, converting them to single long reads","addition_date":"2017-01-13T13:14:36Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:26:32.217431Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:flash","credit":[{"email":"flash.comment@gmail.com","name":"FLASh team","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["ELIXIR-EE"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Read pre-processing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3219"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0310"},{"term":"Sequence merging","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0232"}]}],"name":"FLASH","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"seqwiki_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btr507","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: Next-generation sequencing technologies generate very large numbers of short reads. Even with very deep genome coverage, short read lengths cause problems in de novo assemblies. The use of paired-end libraries with a fragment size shorter than twice the read length provides an opportunity to generate much longer reads by overlapping and merging read pairs before assembling a genome. Results: We present FLASH, a fast computational tool to extend the length of short reads by overlapping paired-end reads from fragment libraries that are sufficiently short. We tested the correctness of the tool on one million simulated read pairs, and we then applied it as a pre-processor for genome assemblies of Illumina reads from the bacterium Staphylococcus aureus and human chromosome 14. FLASH correctly extended and merged reads >99% of the time on simulated reads with an error rate of <1%. With adequately set parameters, FLASH correctly merged reads over 90% of the time even when the reads contained up to 5% errors. When FLASH was used to extend reads prior to assembly, the resulting assemblies had substantially greater N50 lengths for both contigs and scaffolds. \u00a9 The Author 2011. Published by Oxford University Press. All rights reserved.","authors":[{"name":"Magoc T."},{"name":"Salzberg S.L."}],"citationCount":10908,"date":"2011-11-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"FLASH: Fast length adjustment of short reads to improve genome assemblies"},"pmcid":"PMC3198573","pmid":"21903629"}],"topic":[{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0196"},{"term":"Sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3168"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"FLASH","home":"https://bio.tools/flash","summary":"Identifies paired-end reads which overlap in the middle, converting them to single long reads","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"galaxy":{"version":"@VERSION@.4","first_commit":"2017-09-25","conda_name":"flash","conda_version":"1.2.11","summary":"Fast Length Adjustment of SHort reads","edam_operations":["Read pre-processing","Sequence merging","Sequence assembly"],"edam_topics":["Sequencing","Sequence assembly"],"toolshed_categories":["Assembly","Fastq Manipulation"],"toolshed_id":"flash","users_5_years":675,"users_all_time":1113,"usage_5_years":47504,"usage_all_time":58032,"bio_tools_summary":"Identifies paired-end reads which overlap in the middle, converting them to single long reads","bio_tools_ids":"fl